# Scratch Expo 1.0

Active product is `mobile/` (Expo + Expo Router). `ScratchWorkout/` Swift is a **logic oracle** — port types and store behavior, do not copy UI, motion, or Inter/lime chrome.

## In 1.0

- Tabs: Workout, Plans, History, Settings
- Plan-first: no empty / ad-hoc workouts
- Compact plan editor (exercise name, sets, reps per set — weights only while logging)
- Live logging: previous values, check-off, rest timer, auto-advance
- Bundled exercise catalog + custom exercises
- Short onboarding (welcome, kg/lbs)
- Paywall after the first completed workout
- Local persistence only

## Out of 1.0

- Custom page transitions, swipe flourishes, achievement overlays
- Heatmap, hero metrics, seven tracking modes
- ExerciseDB / AscendAPI in production
- Supabase, Sign in with Apple, cloud sync
- Designing screens in Paper first (Paper only for onboarding/paywall if no analog)

## Stack

Expo Router native stack + native tabs, TypeScript, MMKV or SQLite, FlashList, RevenueCat, expo-haptics, `expo-mcp`. No NativeWind, no Inter, no custom tab bar.
